# Documentation rules

- `docs/` contains the 9 user-facing docs (overview, architecture,
  local-setup, build-and-run, provider-setup, prompt-schema,
  runtime-subsystems, project-layout, troubleshooting). All of them MUST
  remain current.
- When code structure changes, update:
  - `docs/architecture.md` if data flow changes,
  - `docs/runtime-subsystems.md` if engine modules change,
  - `docs/prompt-schema.md` if any schema changes,
  - `docs/build-and-run.md` if the build / launch command changes,
  - `docs/troubleshooting.md` if a new reproducible failure has a workaround.
- The `README.md` must always end with a `# Manual Steps I Still Need To Do`
  section that honestly lists software, keys, env vars, and blocked items.
